{
  "@context": "../../context.jsonld",
  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Fabrication and bonding of the solid motor pressure vessel to the cast propellant grain. Steel cases (Maraging steel, 6Al-4V titanium for smaller motors) are machined and welded; composite cases are filament-wound from carbon fiber/epoxy or aramid/epoxy over a mandrel and oven-cured. The liner-insulated case serves directly as the propellant mold in case-bonded designs, eliminating free volume and transferring combustion pressure loads directly into the composite overwrap.",
  "early_win": false,
  "id": "launch-vehicles.solid-propulsion.case-bonding",
